            <ArticleTitle>Cavernous hemangioma presenting as a right adnexal mass in a child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>311-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is the case of an 11-year-old girl who presented with a right adnexal mass and vague abdominal symptoms since seven months prior to her hospital admission for surgery. CT-scan and sonographic images were those of a benign lesion, probably ovarian torsion or infarction. Serum tumoral markers were normal. A right salpingo-oophorectomy and appendectomy were performed. Pathology examination revealed a cavernous hemangioma of the ovary. The clinicopathologic presentation of this unusual benign ovarian tumor is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
